  "subtitle": "One button. Any sound. Now play it.",
  "why_scout_cares": "A $99.95 consumer keyboard where the defining interaction is holding one button, making a noise, and releasing — your sound is now a playable instrument across 32 miniature keys. 1.4 seconds of 8-bit sampling, no menus, no editing. The physical ritual of pointing the device at a sound source and capturing it with a single gesture makes the SK-1 the most accessible sampler ever built. It also became the ur-circuit-bending platform: open the case, touch exposed PCB traces with bare fingers, and the device glitches into a new instrument. Used by Autechre, Blur, DJ Hype, Large Professor. 3 CC-licensed images available on Commons.",
